  ║                    CTaskComplex STATE MACHINE                              ║
  ╠════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      ║
  ║  │ CTaskComplex has THREE key virtual methods:                      │      ║
  ║  │                                                                  │      ║
  ║  │  1. CreateFirstSubTask(CPed*) → CTask*                           │      ║
  ║  │     Called ONCE when task is first set                           │      ║
  ║  │     Returns first subtask to execute                             │      ║
  ║  │                                                                  │      ║
  ║  │  2. ControlSubTask(CPed*) → CTask*                               │      ║
  ║  │     Called EVERY FRAME                                           │      ║
  ║  │     Returns:                                                     │      ║
  ║  │       - Same subtask → Continue current subtask                  │      ║
  ║  │       - Different task → Abort old, start new subtask            │      ║
  ║  │       - nullptr → This complex task is finished                  │      ║
  ║  │                                                                  │      ║
  ║  │  3. CreateNextSubTask(CPed*) → CTask*                            │      ║
  ║  │     Called when current subtask finishes (ProcessPed returns     │      ║
  ║  │     true)                                                        │      ║
  ║  │     Returns:                                                     │      ║
  ║  │       - New subtask → Execute it next                            │      ║
  ║  │       - nullptr → This complex task is finished                  │      ║
  ║  │                                                                  │      ║
  ║  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      ║
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  EXAMPLE: CTaskComplexKillPedOnFoot                                        ║
  ║  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      ║
  ║  │                                                                  │      ║
  ║  │  CreateFirstSubTask() → CTaskComplexSeekEntity (approach target) │      ║
  ║  │           │                                                      │      ║
  ║  │           ▼ (finished approaching)                               │      ║
  ║  │  CreateNextSubTask() → CTaskComplexKillPedOnFootMelee            │      ║
  ║  │           │            OR CTaskSimpleUseGun                      │      ║
  ║  │           ▼                                                      │      ║
  ║  │  ControlSubTask() checks:                                        │      ║
  ║  │    - Target dead? → return nullptr (finished)                    │      ║
  ║  │    - Target fled? → return SeekEntity (chase again)              │      ║
  ║  │    - In range?    → return current attack subtask                │      ║
  ║  │                                                                  │      ║
  ║  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      ║
  ║                                                                            ║
