  ║                    COMPLETE DATA FLOW EXAMPLE                              ║
  ║                    (Ped Gets Punched by Player)                            ║
  ╠════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  1. TRIGGER: Player punches NPC                                            ║
  ║     └── Game creates CEventDamage with source=player, weapon=fist          ║
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  2. EVENT ADDED: CEventGroup::Add(CEventDamage)                            ║
  ║     └── Event queued with priority based on damage severity                ║
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  3. NEXT FRAME: CPedIntelligence::Process()                                ║
  ║     └── m_eventHandler.HandleEvents()                                      ║
  ║         └── Gets CEventDamage as highest priority                          ║
  ║         └── TakesPriorityOverCurrentEvent() = true                         ║
  ║         └── Aborts current wander task                                     ║
  ║         └── ComputeEventResponseTask(CEventDamage)                         ║
  ║             └── ComputeDamageResponse()                                    ║
  ║                 ├── m_PhysicalResponseTask = CTaskSimpleBeHit (flinch)     ║
  ║                 └── ComputePersonalityResponseToDamage()                   ║
  ║                     └── m_EventResponseTask = CTaskComplexKillPedOnFoot    ║
  ║         └── SetEventResponseTask()                                         ║
  ║             ├── TASK_PRIMARY_PHYSICAL_RESPONSE = CTaskSimpleBeHit          ║
  ║             └── TASK_PRIMARY_EVENT_RESPONSE_NONTEMP =                      ║
  ║                                         CTaskComplexKillPedOnFoot          ║
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  4. TASK EXECUTION: m_TaskMgr.ManageTasks()                                ║
  ║     └── Active task = PHYSICAL_RESPONSE (highest priority with task)       ║
  ║     └── CTaskSimpleBeHit::ProcessPed()                                     ║
  ║         └── Plays flinch animation                                         ║
  ║         └── Returns true when animation complete                           ║
  ║     └── Task deleted, nullptr in slot                                      ║
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  5. NEXT FRAME:                                                            ║
  ║     └── Active task = EVENT_RESPONSE_NONTEMP (next priority)               ║
  ║     └── CTaskComplexKillPedOnFoot::CreateFirstSubTask()                    ║
  ║         └── Returns CTaskComplexSeekEntity(player)                         ║
  ║     └── NPC starts approaching player to attack                            ║
  ║                                                                            ║
  ║  6. COMBAT LOOP:                                                           ║
  ║     └── ControlSubTask() monitors distance                                 ║
  ║     └── When in range: CreateNextSubTask() → CTaskSimpleFight              ║
  ║     └── CTaskSimpleFight sets TASK_SECONDARY_ATTACK                        ║
  ║     └── ProcessPed() executes punches/kicks                                ║
  ║                                                                            ║
